title: 'fix(warp sync): do not import the headers of a warp proof'
doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Warp sync no longer imports the headers of a warp proof. It verifies the proof and continues
      with the target block; gap sync delivers these blocks together with their justifications,
      like the rest of the history.

      The imported headers were sparse and reached the client without their justifications and
      without an authority set change recorded by GRANDPA, so they did not make the node able to
      serve warp proofs. Having them in the database caused three failures:

      - On chains whose engine sets the fork choice only in its verifier, such as AURA with
        GRANDPA, every such header failed with `IncompletePipeline`, because these headers skip
        the verifier.
      - When the target directly followed an authority set change, its parent was one of these
        headers. The target is imported as finalized, the client then tried to finalize the parent
        as well and failed with `UnknownBlock`, and warp sync fell back to full sync.
      - GRANDPA block import treats a block that is already stored as processed and drops its
        justification, so gap sync could not add the justification and the authority set change
        later. A node that warp synced answered warp proof requests with `Missing required data`
        or with a proof that skipped authority set changes.

      No API change.
crates:
  - name: sc-network-sync
    bump: patch
